                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Can you please add a `Fixes:` tag pointing to the change that introduced the bug?\n\n```\nFixes: 8836784f1e06 (\"dsp: base: Add encode req & decode resp for MultipartReceive command\")\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 29,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi @john.chung@arm.com, can you please also weigh in?\n\nLooking at the `encode_base_multipart_receive_resp` API, it's only encoding the checksum field in END and START_AND_END part, which also contradicts to the spec where it says:\n\n> DataIntegrityChecksum\n32-bit cumulative CRC for the entirety of data received so far for this section (all parts concatenated together, excluding checksums). **Shall be included with all part transfers**."
                },
                {
                    "file": "CHANGELOG.md",
                    "line": 66,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Easiest to just use the commit subject here:\n\n```\n- dsp: base: Don't extract MultipartReceive resp's CRC once complete\n```\n\nHowever, this should go in the `### Fixed` section below, rather than `### Changed` as you have it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "CHANGELOG.md",
                    "line": 66,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "Moved to the Fixed section with a simple description."
                }
            ],
